      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-104297",
        "knowledge_point_id": "b194bf2f-feaa-5656-a3ee-0ff466a39e77",
        "knowledge_point": "Differentiating a Product Containing a Trigonometric Function",
        "problem": "Differentiate ${e}^{x}cos⁡x.$",
        "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=cos⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}cos⁡x)^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{′}\\cdot cos⁡x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (cos⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(cos⁡x)+({e}^{x})(-sin⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}cos⁡x-{e}^{x}sin⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
