      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-70667",
        "knowledge_point_id": "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7",
        "knowledge_point": "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function",
        "problem": "Which of the following statements regarding the graph of $y=cos⁡x$ are true?\n\n- The graph intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1$\n- The function has a minimum value at $x=-\\pi .$\n- The range of the function is $[-\\pi ,\\pi ].$",
        "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933487/assets/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The $y$-intercepts of the function is $y=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function at $x=-\\pi $ has a minimum value.\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$",
