        "knowledge_point_id": "3c547746-49c8-5a4a-85fe-c6b75493a354",
        "knowledge_point": "Differentiating a Quotient Containing Other Functions",
        "problem": "If $f(x)=\\frac{sin⁡x}{{x}^{2}},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$",
        "worked_solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=sin⁡x$ and $v(x)={x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(sin⁡x)^{′}\\cdot {x}^{2}-sin⁡x\\cdot ({x}^{2})^{′}}{({x}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}cos⁡x-2xsin⁡x}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(xcos⁡x-2sin⁡x)}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{xcos⁡x-2sin⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
